{"title":"Career Roadmap: Network Security Executive","role":"Network Security Executive","summary":"A Network Security Executive helps protect an organization's networks, systems and communications infrastructure from unauthorized access, malware, attacks and security incidents.","facts":{"Current degree":"BCA","Course":"Cyber Security / Ethical Hacking"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build expertise in network architecture, security controls, monitoring, threat detection and incident response"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Network Security Executive helps protect an organization's networks, systems and communications infrastructure from unauthorized access, malware, attacks and security incidents."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer networking"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Firewalls"},{"text":"IDS/IPS"},{"text":"VPNs"},{"text":"Security monitoring"},{"text":"Vulnerability management"},{"text":"Incident response"},{"text":"SIEM"},{"text":"Cloud networking"},{"text":"Basic ethical hacking"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest entry-level profile is not simply someone who knows penetration-testing tools. It is someone who understands how networks work, how they are secured, how attacks appear in network traffic, and how to investigate and respond to incidents."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Networking + Linux foundations"},{"text":"TCP/IP, Linux, programming"},{"text":"Network labs"},{"text":"Using security tools without understanding networking"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Firewalls, VPN, IDS/IPS, access control"},{"text":"Security lab projects"},{"text":"Ignoring network architecture"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Monitoring + incident response"},{"text":"SIEM, logs, Wireshark, threat detection"},{"text":"SOC/network-security projects"},{"text":"Only learning offensive tools"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Enterprise security"},{"text":"Cloud security, automation, threat hunting"},{"text":"Internship + capstone"},{"text":"No real-world incident investigation experience"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer fundamentals"},{"text":"Programming fundamentals"},{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Linux basics"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Operating-system fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Build networking foundations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OSI model"},{"text":"TCP/IP model"},{"text":"IPv4/IPv6"},{"text":"Subnetting"},{"text":"MAC addresses"},{"text":"ARP"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"DHCP"},{"text":"HTTP/HTTPS"},{"text":"TCP/UDP"},{"text":"Routing"},{"text":"Switching"},{"text":"NAT"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice using network simulators and controlled lab environments."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Linux administration"},{"text":"Network architecture"},{"text":"VLANs"},{"text":"Routing protocols"},{"text":"Wireless networking"},{"text":"Network troubleshooting"},{"text":"Basic network automation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cisco networking concepts"},{"text":"Routing and switching fundamentals"},{"text":"Firewall architecture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Start network security:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Firewalls"},{"text":"ACLs"},{"text":"VPNs"},{"text":"IDS"},{"text":"IPS"},{"text":"Network segmentation"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"AAA"},{"text":"Secure protocols"},{"text":"Network hardening"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Security monitoring"},{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"Network traffic analysis"},{"text":"Vulnerability management"},{"text":"SIEM"},{"text":"Log analysis"},{"text":"Threat intelligence"},{"text":"Incident response"},{"text":"Security operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SOC operations"},{"text":"Threat hunting"},{"text":"Malware traffic indicators"},{"text":"Detection engineering"},{"text":"Network forensics"},{"text":"Cloud networking"},{"text":"Cloud security"},{"text":"Python security automation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 7"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a specialization:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Network defense"},{"text":"SOC/security monitoring"},{"text":"Network penetration testing"},{"text":"Cloud network security"},{"text":"Firewall engineering"},{"text":"Network forensics"},{"text":"Threat hunting"},{"text":"Security automation"},{"text":"Zero Trust networking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 8"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industry internship"},{"text":"Network-security capstone"},{"text":"Security portfolio"},{"text":"Resume"},{"text":"Interview preparation"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Networking Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Network Security Executive must be strong in networking before specializing in security."},{"type":"h","text":"TCP/IP"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IP addressing"},{"text":"Subnetting"},{"text":"Routing"},{"text":"TCP"},{"text":"UDP"},{"text":"Ports"},{"text":"Sockets"},{"text":"NAT"},{"text":"ICMP"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Protocols"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the security implications of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HTTP/HTTPS"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"DHCP"},{"text":"SSH"},{"text":"FTP/SFTP"},{"text":"SMTP"},{"text":"IMAP"},{"text":"LDAP"},{"text":"SMB"},{"text":"SNMP"},{"text":"NTP"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Network Devices"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Routers"},{"text":"Switches"},{"text":"Firewalls"},{"text":"Load balancers"},{"text":"Proxies"},{"text":"Wireless access points"},{"text":"VPN gateways"},{"text":"IDS/IPS"},{"text":"Network taps"}]}]},{"heading":"Network Security","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how organizations protect network infrastructure."},{"type":"h","text":"Firewalls"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Packet filtering"},{"text":"Stateful inspection"},{"text":"Application-aware filtering"},{"text":"ACLs"},{"text":"NAT"},{"text":"Firewall rules"},{"text":"Logging"},{"text":"Network zones"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Enterprise technologies may include platforms such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Palo Alto Networks"},{"text":"Fortinet"},{"text":"Cisco"},{"text":"Check Point"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact platform depends on the employer."},{"type":"h","text":"Network Segmentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"VLANs"},{"text":"DMZ"},{"text":"Internal segmentation"},{"text":"Micro-segmentation"},{"text":"Network access control"},{"text":"Zero Trust concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"VPN"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Site-to-site VPN"},{"text":"Remote-access VPN"},{"text":"IPsec"},{"text":"TLS-based VPN concepts"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Encryption"},{"text":"Tunnelling"}]}]},{"heading":"IDS & IPS","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"IDS"},{"type":"h","text":"Intrusion Detection System"},{"type":"p","text":"Detects suspicious activity and generates alerts."},{"type":"h","text":"IPS"},{"type":"h","text":"Intrusion Prevention System"},{"type":"p","text":"Can actively block or prevent malicious traffic."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Signature-based detection"},{"text":"Anomaly detection"},{"text":"Network-based IDS"},{"text":"Host-based IDS"},{"text":"Alert analysis"},{"text":"False positives"},{"text":"Detection rules"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools/platforms to explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Snort"},{"text":"Suricata"},{"text":"Zeek"}]}]},{"heading":"Network Monitoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to investigate network activity."},{"type":"h","text":"Wireshark"},{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Packet capture"},{"text":"Protocol analysis"},{"text":"TCP streams"},{"text":"DNS traffic"},{"text":"HTTP traffic"},{"text":"TLS handshakes"},{"text":"Suspicious connections"},{"text":"Packet filtering"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example filters:"},{"type":"p","text":"tcp"},{"type":"p","text":"udp"},{"type":"p","text":"dns"},{"type":"p","text":"http"},{"type":"p","text":"icmp"},{"type":"p","text":"tcp.port == 443"},{"type":"p","text":"ip.addr == x.x.x.x"},{"type":"h","text":"Network Traffic Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Port scanning"},{"text":"Brute-force indicators"},{"text":"Suspicious DNS"},{"text":"Beaconing"},{"text":"Unusual outbound traffic"},{"text":"Large data transfers"},{"text":"Command-and-control indicators"},{"text":"Abnormal authentication patterns"}]},{"type":"p","text":"All testing should be performed on systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess."}]},{"heading":"SIEM & Security Monitoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the fundamentals of Security Information and Event Management."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Log collection"},{"text":"Log normalization"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Alerting"},{"text":"Dashboards"},{"text":"Detection rules"},{"text":"Incident investigation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Platforms worth learning:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft Sentinel"},{"text":"Splunk"},{"text":"IBM QRadar"},{"text":"Elastic Security"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You don't need all of them. One platform learned deeply is a better starting point."}]},{"heading":"Incident Response","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn a structured incident-response process:"},{"type":"h","text":"Preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Detection"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Containment"},{"type":"h","text":"Eradication"},{"type":"h","text":"Recovery"},{"type":"h","text":"Lessons Learned"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how network evidence contributes to each phase."},{"type":"p","text":"Practice investigating:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Suspicious login"},{"text":"Malware communication"},{"text":"Port scanning"},{"text":"Phishing-related traffic"},{"text":"Credential attacks"},{"text":"Unauthorized remote access"},{"text":"Data exfiltration indicators"}]}]},{"heading":"Vulnerability Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Asset discovery"},{"text":"Vulnerability identification"},{"text":"CVE concepts"},{"text":"CVSS concepts"},{"text":"Patch management"},{"text":"Configuration weaknesses"},{"text":"Risk prioritization"},{"text":"Remediation verification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nessus"},{"text":"OpenVAS/Greenbone"},{"text":"Nmap"},{"text":"Qualys concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A vulnerability is not automatically a critical business risk; learn to consider exploitability, exposure, asset importance and business impact."}]},{"heading":"Ethical Hacking Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Although the target is network security rather than penetration testing, basic offensive knowledge is valuable."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reconnaissance"},{"text":"Port scanning"},{"text":"Service enumeration"},{"text":"Vulnerability identification"},{"text":"Authentication weaknesses"},{"text":"Network misconfiguration"},{"text":"Web-security fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nmap"},{"text":"Burp Suite"},{"text":"Metasploit"},{"text":"Kali Linux"},{"text":"Nikto"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is to understand how attackers discover weaknesses so defenders can detect and mitigate them."}]},{"heading":"Linux & System Security","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux filesystem"},{"text":"Users/groups"},{"text":"Permissions"},{"text":"Processes"},{"text":"Services"},{"text":"SSH"},{"text":"System logs"},{"text":"Networking commands"},{"text":"Firewall configuration"},{"text":"Package management"},{"text":"Bash scripting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important commands to understand:"},{"type":"p","text":"ip"},{"type":"p","text":"ss"},{"type":"p","text":"ping"},{"type":"p","text":"traceroute"},{"type":"p","text":"dig"},{"type":"p","text":"nslookup"},{"type":"p","text":"curl"},{"type":"p","text":"wget"},{"type":"p","text":"tcpdump"},{"type":"p","text":"netstat"},{"type":"p","text":"journalctl"},{"type":"p","text":"systemctl"},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn Windows security fundamentals:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Active Directory"},{"text":"Domain controllers"},{"text":"Group Policy"},{"text":"Windows event logs"},{"text":"Kerberos concepts"},{"text":"LDAP"},{"text":"NTLM concepts"},{"text":"Windows Defender"}]}]},{"heading":"Cloud Network Security","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern network-security roles increasingly require cloud knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"AWS"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"VPC"},{"text":"Subnets"},{"text":"Route tables"},{"text":"Security groups"},{"text":"Network ACLs"},{"text":"Internet/NAT gateways"},{"text":"VPN"},{"text":"Cloud logging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Azure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Virtual networks"},{"text":"NSGs"},{"text":"Azure Firewall"},{"text":"Private endpoints"},{"text":"VPN"},{"text":"Microsoft Sentinel"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cloud segmentation"},{"text":"Zero Trust"},{"text":"IAM"},{"text":"Security monitoring"},{"text":"Cloud logging"},{"text":"Network security posture"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You don't need to master every cloud provider initially."}]},{"heading":"Python for Security","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Use Python for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Log processing"},{"text":"Network automation"},{"text":"API integration"},{"text":"Security reports"},{"text":"IOC processing"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Alert enrichment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful libraries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"requests"},{"text":"socket"},{"text":"scapy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"json"},{"text":"re"},{"text":"paramiko"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn basic Bash scripting and optionally PowerShell."}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Network Monitoring Lab"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a controlled network environment containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux machines"},{"text":"Windows machine"},{"text":"Router/firewall"},{"text":"Web server"},{"text":"Monitoring system"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Capture traffic with Wireshark and analyze normal vs suspicious activity."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Network Intrusion Detection Lab"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Traffic","IDS","Alerts","SIEM","Investigation Dashboard"]},{"type":"p","text":"Use technologies such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Suricata or Snort"},{"text":"Zeek"},{"text":"Elastic/Splunk"},{"text":"Wireshark"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create detection scenarios for authorized lab traffic and document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Detection"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Severity"},{"text":"Investigation"},{"text":"Response"},{"text":"Remediation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Vulnerability & Network Security Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an authorized lab assessment covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Asset discovery"},{"text":"Port/service identification"},{"text":"Vulnerability scanning"},{"text":"Risk classification"},{"text":"Configuration review"},{"text":"Remediation recommendations"},{"text":"Verification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a professional security assessment report."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Enterprise Network Security Monitoring Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an end-to-end defensive security environment."},{"type":"h","text":"Architecture"},{"type":"h","text":"Network Traffic"},{"type":"h","text":"Zeek / Suricata"},{"type":"h","text":"Log Collection"},{"type":"h","text":"SIEM"},{"type":"h","text":"Detection Rules"},{"type":"h","text":"Security Dashboard"},{"type":"h","text":"Incident Investigation"},{"type":"h","text":"Response Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Network topology"},{"text":"Asset inventory"},{"text":"Firewall policy"},{"text":"IDS/IPS"},{"text":"SIEM"},{"text":"Alert prioritization"},{"text":"Threat intelligence"},{"text":"Incident tickets"},{"text":"Security dashboard"},{"text":"Automated notifications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Optional:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python automation"},{"text":"ML-based anomaly detection"},{"text":"Cloud network monitoring"}]}]},{"heading":"Specialization Choices","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialization","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Network Defense"},{"text":"Firewalls, IDS/IPS, segmentation"}],[{"text":"SOC"},{"text":"Monitoring, detection, incident response"}],[{"text":"Network Forensics"},{"text":"Packet and traffic investigation"}],[{"text":"Firewall Engineering"},{"text":"Enterprise firewall architecture"}],[{"text":"Cloud Network Security"},{"